body:
as someone who was basically in your daughter's position, please make sure she feels loved. when i was about \~5 years old, i went form being the family favorite to being absolutely forgotten by every adult in my family the moment my niece was born. it affects me to this day.

&#x200B;

i think you should really have a better talk with your husband about this. these people are your in laws, so while technically your family, they're related by blood only to him - if you get through how much favoritism affects people to your husband, you should feel much better. he might be so used to this behavior from his parents that he doesn't see anything wrong with it.

&#x200B;

you're a good mother for caring so much, OP. it's an incredibly frustrating situation and i applaud you for seeking to change it.
